  my 1/V_max HIMF vs the published one: median ratio 1.11 over log M_HI = 8.9-10.3, but the faint-end slope comes out alpha = -1.66 against the published -1.29
  [PASS] 32.4 AGAINST MY OWN ESTIMATOR: a 1/V_max mass function built here from the same catalogue matches the published one in the middle but is far too steep at the faint end -- the known large-scale-structure bias of 1/V_max, which is exactly why the published 2D-stepwise functions were used for the test above and not this.  If section 2 had been run on my own 1/V_max the framework's predicted slope would have been -2.3, spuriously   (my alpha = -1.66 vs published -1.29; middle-decade amplitude ratio 1.11)

